{"source":"The shared printer has made a noticeable difference to the workshop. Students can now test small parts without travelling to the main building, which is particularly helpful during evening sessions. There have also been problems: the booking sheet is often out of date, and failed prints are sometimes left in the tray without a note.

My view is that we should keep the printer here and fix the management of it. Moving it back would solve the untidy tray by making the machine less useful. A named person for each evening, plus a simple record of failed jobs, seems a more proportionate response.","candidate":"The shared printer has made a noticeable difference to the workshop. Students can now test small parts without travelling to the main building, which is particularly helpful during evening sessions. There have also been problems: the booking sheet is often out of date, and failed prints are sometimes left in the tray without a note.

